# ============================================================================
# UofA mrm-nist pack — Group B evaluation-sufficiency weakeners (NIST AI 800-3)
# ============================================================================
# Spec:   docs/model-credibility-pack-spec.md §3 (+ addenda v0.1 §A1/§A2)
# Engine: Apache Jena GenericRuleReasoner (FORWARD_RETE mode)
# Pack:   mrm-nist v0.2.0
#
# These rules assess a *reported benchmark result* as validation evidence. The
# node they fire on is uofa:ValidationResult -- the SAME node type vv40 uses for
# a simulation validation study. That reuse is the point: a benchmark result is
# validation evidence about a model, not a new kind of thing (pack spec §6).
#
# ── The firewall, and why it needs no dispatcher ────────────────────────────
# Every rule below binds (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr) in its body. A
# model with a card but no reported evaluation has no such node, so these rules
# structurally CANNOT fire -- zero Group-B weakeners, not N failures. The
# firewall is a property of the rule bodies, not of a suppression step. Do not
# "optimize" a rule by dropping that clause; it is load-bearing.
# Guarded by tests/test_group_b_firewall.py, which must be made to fail on
# purpose when edited (AGENTS.md §13).
#
# ── What is deliberately NOT here ──────────────────────────────────────────
# W-EV-UQ-01 was withdrawn. Core's W-AL-01 already fires on
# noValue(?result, uofa:hasUncertaintyQuantification) for any ValidationResult,
# and mrm-nist runs all 23 core patterns -- so a second rule would report one
# missing standard error twice under two IDs. The adapter populates core's
# property instead, and W-AL-01 fires unchanged on an LLM benchmark exactly as
# it does on a blood-pump CFD study. Seven other core rules also bind
# hasValidationResult and legitimately fire on these nodes (notably W-AR-05:
# raidex furnishes no comparator at all).
#
# BECAUSE core rules fire per node, the reporting layer MUST aggregate by
# patternId with an affected-node count. Ten validation results must not become
# ten rows.
#
# ── Absence is tested, never a falsy value ─────────────────────────────────
# Every noValue() below assumes the extractor OMITS a property it cannot
# furnish. Emitting `false` or "N/A" would make the triple exist and silence the
# rule -- the failure mode AGENTS.md §13 describes as satisfying a constraint
# with a plausible value. tests/test_group_b_rule_property_coverage.py pins the
# rule-tested properties against what the adapter can emit.
# ============================================================================

@prefix uofa: <https://uofa.net/vocab#>.
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/>.

# ============================================================================
# SIMPLE WEAKENERS
# ============================================================================

# W-EV-GEN-02: Benchmark accuracy presented without a superpopulation account.
# 800-3's core distinction: benchmark accuracy is accuracy ON THE BENCHMARK.
# Treating it as generalized accuracy requires stating how the items relate to
# the target population. raidex furnishes n_samples but no such account, so this
# fires across the cohort -- that IS the finding, not a calibration error.
[w_ev_gen02:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:samplingAccount)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-GEN-02', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-GEN-02')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Reported benchmark score carries no account of how its items sample the target population - benchmark accuracy cannot be read as generalized accuracy.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-DET-03: No per-model determinism floor / reproducibility statement.
# Grounding: Seahaven TRAP 35. An eval score without a stated temperature, seed,
# or repeat-run spread is a single draw reported as a measurement.
[w_ev_det03:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:harnessDeterminismStatement)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-DET-03', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-DET-03')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Reported evaluation states no determinism floor - sampling settings and per-model run-to-run spread are uncharacterized, so the score is one draw reported as a measurement.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-NULL-04: Score not calibrated against a null / chance baseline.
# Grounding: the Seahaven null-calibration work. Distinct from core's W-AR-05
# (noValue comparedAgainst): a comparator is the data a result was validated
# against; a null baseline is the comprehension-free floor the score must clear.
# A result can carry one without the other, which is why these stay separate.
[w_ev_null04:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:nullBaselineStatement)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-NULL-04', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-NULL-04')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Reported score is not calibrated against a null, chance, or comprehension-free baseline - the floor the score must clear to mean anything is unstated.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-CAP-06: Capability confound not partialled.
# Grounding: the Seahaven capability-confound finding. A separation attributable
# to general capability rather than to the measured construct is not evidence
# about the construct.
[w_ev_cap06:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:confoundControlStatement)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-CAP-06', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-CAP-06')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'Medium')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'No capability-confound control stated - the reported separation may be attributable to general capability rather than to the construct the benchmark claims to measure.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# ── W-EV-COU-05: no stated context of use, at two severities ───────────────
#
# TWO RULES, ONE patternId. Precedent: w_si02_no_req / w_si02_no_result in core.
#
# THE FINDING IS noValue(?vr, uofa:claimedCOU) -- the PUBLISHED RECORD lacking a
# stated context of use. Both bodies carry that clause. The operator's --cou
# flag only selects the severity; it never creates the finding. A rule that
# discriminated solely on the flag would manufacture a Critical against a model
# whose card properly states its COU, i.e. report on the operator's input
# instead of on the evidence. tests/fixtures/weakeners/W-EV-COU-05/boundary
# pins exactly that case: claimedCOU present AND --cou supplied -> no firing.
#
# uofa:decisionContextOfUse is the RUN-CONTEXT property bound to --cou, and is
# deliberately NOT uofa:hasContextOfUse -- that one is already synthesized from
# the model id on every mrm-nist bundle, so keying on it would take the Critical
# branch unconditionally (addendum v0.1 §A2, patched).
#
# The two bodies are mutually exclusive by construction (one requires
# decisionContextOfUse, the other its absence), so they can never collide on the
# same node -- which is why the Skolem discriminates on ?vr rather than on a
# literal, unlike w_si02_*.

# Critical: an actual decision is on the table and the record does not say the
# benchmark is relevant to it.
[w_ev_cou05_scoped:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:claimedCOU)
    (?uofa uofa:decisionContextOfUse ?dcou)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-COU-05', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-COU-05')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'Critical')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Reported evaluation states no context-of-use relevance, and an assessment context was supplied - the score is being read against a decision the published record never claimed it informs.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# High: the same gap, but no specific decision is being informed. Near-universal
# firing here is accepted as the finding (addendum v0.1 §A2, decision recorded);
# the reporting layer renders it once with a field-prevalence note.
[w_ev_cou05_unscoped:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:claimedCOU)
    noValue(?uofa, uofa:decisionContextOfUse)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-COU-05', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-COU-05')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Reported evaluation states no context-of-use relevance - the decision this score would inform is unstated.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# ============================================================================
# COMPOUND WEAKENERS (fire on Group-B output, chained)
# ============================================================================

# COMPOUND-EV-01: a score drives a high-risk decision AND lacks BOTH uncertainty
# and null calibration -> Critical escalation.
#
# uofa:decisionRiskLevel is the RUN-CONTEXT property bound to --mrl. It is
# deliberately NOT uofa:modelRiskLevel, which every mrm-nist bundle already
# carries as the disclosed MRM_NIST_ASSUMED_MRL = 3 posture -- keying on that
# would make greaterThan(?mrl, 2) true for every model and this rule would fire
# unconditionally, which is the dead-rule failure addendum v0.1 §A2 exists to
# prevent. With no --mrl there is no triple, the rule cannot match, and the
# readout states "MRL not supplied - compound risk escalation not assessed."
# The honest N/A is a property of rule structure, not a special case in the
# renderer.
[w_compound_ev01:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    (?uofa uofa:decisionRiskLevel ?mrl)
    greaterThan(?mrl, 2)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:hasUncertaintyQuantification)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:nullBaselineStatement)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'COMPOUND-EV-01', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'COMPOUND-EV-01')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'Critical')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'Score informs a high-risk decision while carrying neither an uncertainty estimate nor a null baseline - there is no basis for judging whether the reported difference is real.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# COMPOUND-EV-02: a generalized performance claim AND no sampling account ->
# the generalization is unsupported by the sample that produced it.
#
# uofa:generalizedClaim marks a result presented as a general/aggregate claim
# rather than a task-specific measurement. The raidex adapter sets it on the
# composite node only (rai_score is definitionally a cross-constituent index),
# never on individual constituents -- so this fires once per model, not ten
# times.
[w_compound_ev02:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    (?vr uofa:generalizedClaim ?g)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:samplingAccount)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'COMPOUND-EV-02', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'COMPOUND-EV-02')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'Critical')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'A generalized performance claim rests on a sample with no stated relationship to the population it generalizes over - the claim is broader than the evidence supporting it.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-SUB-08: the evaluation subject is not configuration-controlled.
#
# Prior to W-EV-DET-03, not a variant of it. DET-03 asks whether sampling
# variance WITHIN a fixed subject is characterized; this asks whether the
# subject was fixed at all. Characterizing run-to-run spread on a subject that
# can change under its own name measures the wrong thing precisely.
#
# Grounding: NASA-STD-7009 configuration-control expectations, applied to the
# measured subject rather than to the model under simulation.
#
# Fires when the ValidationResult carries only a claimed identity -- a
# provider-asserted identifier with no immutable version guarantee (the
# occasion-pin case of addendum v0.2 A9.1). Every API-hosted model qualifies:
# 41 of the 43 published records. Near-universal firing IS the finding, and the
# reporting layer carries a prevalence note, as it does for W-EV-COU-05.
#
# What it says: a closed-weight score is evidence about an OCCASION, not about
# an artifact. It can be re-performed; it cannot be re-derived.
[w_ev_sub08:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    noValue(?vr, uofa:subjectVersionGuarantee)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-SUB-08', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-SUB-08')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'The evaluation subject is not configuration-controlled - its identity is claimed by the provider with no immutable version guarantee, so the score is evidence about an occasion rather than about a fixed artifact.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-COR-09: no independent referent corroborates the reported scores.
#
# Grounding: the V&V multiple-referent tradition -- a result gains credibility
# from agreement with an INDEPENDENT referent, and a single unreplicated referent
# is weaker evidence than a corroborated one. Not a new category.
#
# ── The firewall line this rule sits on, and which side it is written for ──
#
# There are two readings and only one is legitimate:
#
#   (a) "no independent evidence corroborates any reported score" -- a sufficiency
#       statement about the PUBLISHED RECORD. Corroboration was possible to look
#       for and was not found. This is what the rule fires on.
#
#   (b) "the furnisher did not cover this model" -- a fact about the ASSESSOR's
#       roster, not the vendor's record. Firing on that would penalize an absence
#       the vendor never claimed to fill, which is the wall-of-red failure the
#       pack spec forbids.
#
# Reading (b) is excluded STRUCTURALLY, not by wording: the body requires a
# furnished result to exist in the bundle. With no furnisher run, `?other` binds
# nothing and the rule cannot match, so a card-only assessment is silent here and
# the readout states the N/A. The honest absence falls out of rule structure, as
# it does for COMPOUND-EV-01 and W-EV-COU-05.
#
# Severity Medium, deliberately below the missing-property weakeners: nobody did
# anything wrong. The card published what it published and the furnisher measured
# what it measures. The finding is about the EVIDENCE STATE, and the description
# is evidence-shaped rather than fault-shaped for the same reason.
#
# Expected to be the common case: across 49 cards only 8% name any constituent
# raidex measures (studies/card-eval-reporting-2026-08). Cards report capability;
# this furnisher measures responsible-AI properties.
[w_ev_cor09:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    (?vr uofa:evidenceSource 'reported')
    noValue(?vr, uofa:corroboratedBy)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?other)
    (?other uofa:evidenceSource 'furnished')
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-COR-09', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-COR-09')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'Medium')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'No independently furnished measurement corroborates this reported score - the furnished evidence available measures different properties, so the published number stands on a single referent.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]

# W-EV-DIV-07: a reported score disagrees with an independent measurement.
#
# Grounding: V&V40 output comparison, applied to evaluation -- and the §6a
# furnisher/assessor firewall made testable. Where it fires it is the strongest
# finding this pack can produce, because it does not report a missing property
# but a substantive disagreement about a number someone published.
#
# Fires on a MATCHED pair only. `divergesFromFurnished` is set by
# card_prose.match_and_compare when a reported result and a furnished result
# measure the same constituent and differ by more than the tolerance
# (DIV_TOLERANCE_NORMALIZED = 5.0, above the 4.08 cohort maximum standard error;
# the furnished side's own uncertainty is used instead when it states one).
#
# An UNMATCHED reported score never carries the property, so no rule fires: the
# alias table is exact-match only, and a fuzzy match would let "MMLU" reach
# "wmdp" by edit distance and manufacture a disagreement between unrelated
# measurements -- a finding a reader could not tell apart from a real one.
# Silence on an ambiguous match is the correct output.
#
# Expected to be rare: across 49 cards only 8% name any constituent this
# furnisher measures. The disjoint case belongs to W-EV-COR-09, not here.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM. A divergence establishes that the published number and
# an independent run disagree. It does NOT establish which is correct, and the
# description must not imply that it does -- the finding is about the record.
[w_ev_div07:
    (?uofa rdf:type uofa:UnitOfAssurance)
    (?uofa uofa:hasValidationResult ?vr)
    (?vr uofa:divergesFromFurnished ?delta)
    makeSkolem(?ann, ?uofa, 'W-EV-DIV-07', ?vr)
    ->
    (?ann rdf:type uofa:WeakenerAnnotation)
    (?ann uofa:patternId 'W-EV-DIV-07')
    (?ann uofa:severity 'High')
    (?ann uofa:affectedNode ?vr)
    (?ann schema:description 'The score reported in the published record disagrees with an independent measurement of the same benchmark by more than the measurement tolerance - the two do not agree, and which is correct is not established here.')
    (?uofa uofa:hasWeakener ?ann)
]
